node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
*.log

# `scripts/pack-legal.ts` copies the root LICENSE and NOTICE into each package from `prepack`, so
# that a tarball carries the terms it is published under — npm ships only what is inside the package
# directory. Committing four copies of each would be committing four things that can disagree with
# the original, and the day they do is the day somebody edited the original.
packages/*/LICENSE
packages/*/NOTICE

# Where wrangler and miniflare keep a local deployment's state and their build scratch. It holds
# the SQLite files a Durable Object was actually written to on this machine, which is several
# megabytes of somebody's last `wrangler dev` and belongs to nobody else: a committed copy would be
# one developer's fleet, replayed as a starting condition into every checkout and every CI run.
.wrangler/

# `wrangler types` writes this from `examples/fleet-worker/wrangler.jsonc`, and it is the runtime
# types for workerd — thirteen thousand lines of Cloudflare's own declarations, none of it this
# repository's prose. It is regenerated by that example's `typecheck` script, so a clean checkout
# has it before `tsc` runs and nothing here has to gate a copy of it for drift.
worker-configuration.d.ts
